xt":"UndirectedEdgeDepthFirstSearch","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/UndirectedEdgeDepthFirstSearch","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The edge depth-first search of an undirected graph: a sequence of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent"},{"type":"text","text":"s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that reports each edge once, by its position, from the end that reaches it first. The tree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge into a vertex is not reported again from it, so a parallel edge to the parent is a back"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge. It holds a copy of the graph and can be iterated more than once, and keeps its own stack."}]}}}